PART OF CANVAS
--------------

This repository holds the shared packages of the Canvas open layer and the
canvas-edge device runtime. The client applications live in their own
repositories (canvas-web, canvas-cli, canvas-desktop,
canvas-browser-extension; until 2026-10 they were `apps/*` here).

    packages/protocol           wire contract (envelope, codes, routes, events)
    packages/schemas            document schema ids, versions, builders
    packages/api-client         REST client over the protocol package

This repository is one component of the Canvas project:

    this repository  https://github.com/canvas-ui/canvas-common
    the project      https://github.com/canvas-ui/canvas-server

Canvas components are not all licensed the same way. The server runtime and
the services behind it (canvas-server, canvas-synapsd, canvas-stored,
canvas-inferd, canvas-agentd) are dual-licensed: AGPL-3.0-or-later or a
commercial licence. The shared libraries in this repository (`packages/*`)
are dual-licensed the same way. The client applications (formerly `apps/*`
here, now their own repositories), and the canvas-fuse client, are AGPL-only. The COMPONENTS section
of the project NOTICE lists which is which.


DISTRIBUTION
------------

The components in this repository are clients that run on the user's own
machine or in their browser, so the network clause in section 13 of the AGPL
is rarely the one that applies to them. Sections 4 to 6 are. If you convey
these programs, modified or not, through an app store, an extension gallery, a
package registry, a distribution image or an appliance, recipients must
receive this licence and an offer of the corresponding source.

If you build against a modified Canvas server, section 13 reaches that server
too. See the project NOTICE.


